{
  "id": "cloudwatch-asg-live-scaling",
  "name": "CloudWatch \u2192 ASG: Live EC2 Scale-Out",
  "category": "Compute & Auto Scaling",
  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "description": "Live canvas demo: select CloudWatch \u2192 Config to choose target tracking, step scaling, scheduled scaling, or simple scaling. Send Request at Normal traffic twice to breach the initial threshold (120 requests / 2 targets = 60 > 50). EC2 instances appear in the subnet. Scheduled actions use Advance one period / Play scaling independently of requests. Reset scaling before changing policy. Synthetic traffic and accelerated time are teaching inputs.",
  "learningOutcome": "Observe alarm evaluation, desired capacity, EC2 launch and warmup directly on the canvas. Compare proportional target tracking, threshold breach bands, and time-based capacity changes. Initial two instances are retained; target tracking and schedules can remove generated instances.",
